# Hybrid Components & shadcn/ui

## Directory structure

Organize `src/components/` as shared primitives plus feature folders:

```
src/components/
├── ui/              # shadcn primitives (Button, Input, Card, etc.)
├── atoms/           # shared, domain-agnostic primitives and small compositions
└── features/
    ├── leads/       # inbox / membership lead UI
    ├── settings/    # portal settings sections
    ├── portal/      # portal chrome (header, skeleton)
    ├── marketing/   # public site pages, chrome, layouts
    ├── email/       # email product surfaces
    └── contact/     # contact form
```

Features are **flat** — no `molecules/` or `organisms/` nesting inside a feature.

## Layer responsibilities

| Layer | Purpose | Examples |
|-------|---------|----------|
| `ui/` | shadcn-installed primitives — treat as atoms | `Button`, `Input`, `Card` |
| `atoms/` | shared, domain-agnostic elements reused across features | `FadeIn`, `MaterialIcon`, `Select`, `RichTextEditor`, `CodeBlock` |
| `features/<name>/` | anything tied to a product area | `LeadDetail`, `SettingsShell`, `HomePage`, `ContactForm` |

Pages in `src/app/` compose feature components (and shared atoms when needed) — not raw `ui/` primitives for page structure.

## Import direction

Only import **downward**:

`pages` → `features` → `atoms` → `ui`

- Features may import `atoms/` and `ui/` only.
- Do not import one feature from another, except the documented one-way case: `marketing` → `contact` (`ContactForm` inside `ServicesPage`).
- Prefer importing `features/portal/*` from pages/layouts rather than from other features when possible.

## Prefer shadcn

Before building custom UI from scratch:

1. Check the [shadcn/ui docs](https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components) for an existing component.
2. Install it: `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <component>`
3. Import from `@/components/ui/<component>`.
4. Customize with Tailwind classes and `cn()` — compose in `atoms/` or a feature folder; don't fork `ui/` files unless the primitive itself must change.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — compose shadcn primitives in a shared atom or feature
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { Input } from "@/components/ui/input";

export function SearchField() {
  return (
    <div className="flex gap-2">
      <Input placeholder="Search…" />
      <Button type="submit">Search</Button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — reinventing a shadcn primitive
export function CustomButton({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return <button className="rounded-md bg-primary px-4 py-2">{children}</button>;
}
```

## When to use atoms vs features

- **`atoms/`** — domain-agnostic (motion, icons, editors, generic selects). If the name would make sense in another product, it belongs here.
- **`features/<name>/`** — tied to leads, settings, marketing, email, contact, or portal chrome. Prefer a feature folder over inventing new shared layers.
- **`ui/`** — shadcn only.

## File conventions

- PascalCase component names with named exports.
- Colocate stories (`*.stories.tsx`) and tests next to the component.
- Storybook titles: `"Atoms/…"`, `"UI/…"`, or `"Features/<Feature>/…"`.
- Use `@/` path aliases for all imports.
